From 5476876f0f06544f28322d9e5f82073c2c89a4d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Kennedy <nick@nick-kennedy.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:05:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: order stitched final segments before their tail
 commit

When the final segment of a stitched render pass ends in a split, the
rest of that command buffer, including the custom resolve that reads the
multisampled attachments, is committed after the stitched group. Metal
could start it before the merged pass had stored its attachments, so the
resolve read a stale copy: in Alyx the menu and hands, drawn in later
segments, flickered out of the left eye. The queue now signals a shared
event after the stitched group and waits on it before the tail commit.

KK_STITCH_LOG=N logs the encoders of the first N stitched chains.

AI-written commit text (biblioklept).

Generated-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
